        ]
      },
      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Taranga contó a sus hijos antes de bailar: uno, dos, tres, cuatro… ¿y cinco?",
          "en": "Before the dance, Taranga counted her sons: one, two, three, four… and five?"
        },
        {
          "es": "«¿Y tú de dónde saliste?», preguntó. «Tú no eres hijo mío.»",
          "en": "'And where did you come from?' she asked. 'You are not my child.'"
        },
        {
          "es": "Entonces Māui le contó su historia: el moño de pelo, el mar, las algas y el antepasado del cielo.",
          "en": "So Māui told her his story: the knot of hair, the sea, the seaweed, and the ancestor in the sky."
        },
        {
          "es": "Taranga lo escuchó asombrada. «Eres mi último hijo», le dijo.",
          "en": "Taranga listened in wonder. 'You are my last-born son,' she said."
        },
        {
          "es": "«Te llamarás Māui-tikitiki-a-Taranga: Māui, el del moño de Taranga.»",
          "en": "'You will be called Māui-tikitiki-a-Taranga: Māui of Taranga's topknot.'"
        },
        {
          "es": "Esa noche lo dejó dormir a su lado, y sus hermanos se pusieron celosos.",
          "en": "That night she let him sleep beside her, and his brothers grew jealous."
        }
      ],
